4. One-dimensional approach
4.1. Introduction
As recalled above, provided the roughness element height is not too large compared to the boundary layer thickness, the outer region is affected by wall roughness only through the change in friction and heat flux levels. Moreover, RANS approaches have the nice, although unphysical, property to provide a unique solution in the inner region whatever the Reynolds number, once written in wall units. These two facts allow us to reduce the problem to the solution of the discrete element approach equations in the wall region, i.e. to a very simple, one-dimensional system.
